<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korea's January energy demand up 5 pct.</title>
<headline>South Korea's January energy demand up 5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's energy demand rose five percent to 16.231 million tonnes of oil equivalent (TOE) in January year-on-year, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The breakdown of South Korea's January demand for energy resources, compared with the same month last year (figures in brackets are year-on-year growth in percentage):</p>
<p>				  Jan 1997		 Jan 1996</p>
<p>				Amount		 Amount</p>
<p> Total			16,231  (5.0)	15,461   (9.3)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 TOE) </p>
<p> Petroleum products     73,624   (1.2)	72,784   (7.3)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 barrels)</p>
<p> LNG			   1,412  (51.5)	   932  (19.6)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Hard coal		     348  (21.4)	   443 (-19.0)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Bituminous coal	   3,571   (2.1)	 3,497  (14.2)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Nuclear power	     6,085   (2.9)	 5,915  (11.8)</p>
<p>(in gigawatt hours)</p>
<p> Hydroelectric power	 380  (4.7)	    363  (16.8)</p>
<p>(in gigawatt hours)</p>
<p> Other			   103  (18.4)	    87   (2.7)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 TOE)</p>
<p>(Source: Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy)</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
